# followup-image-parity: reduced by the wire audit (t19). Already applied: resvg =0.45.1 in mixdog-imaging, mixdog-js in mixdog-exthost-worker, the lock entries, an AVIF decoder (rav1d =1.1.0).

## Still open
- Image routing: image.* stay with the script worker (compose.rs native_ext_methods filter) until the strict corpus passes; see t6-avif-encode.wire (the AVIF tests still fail). No sniffed-content fallback and no environment toggle. This is a temporary migration blocker, not permission to keep product Node as the final implementation.
- Known document parameter boundary (in-crate, mixdog-ooxml-text extraction options; owner of that crate): the generic handler maxOutputBytes null / negative / fractional / string and non-integer maxPartBytes / maxContainerBytes differ from JS arithmetic and Buffer.subarray; the extraction crate's usize/u64 limit API cannot express negative-relative slicing or preserve the original parameter spelling in the truncation suffix. The real caller (mixdog-tools/src/fs/read.rs) emits a non-negative integer maxOutputBytes, so nothing in use is lost today; no new refusal may be added to close it.
- SVG pixel colours differ from librsvg by up to 2 levels on blended alpha (tests/svg_reference.rs states it): the strict corpus must pass before the SVG subset is called ready (mixdog-raster::twin_svg and the svg tests are in t8-fails.txt).
